        "original_id": "ddb8b60a-260a-5ad4-9b67-46a2dd836f5d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bebe Rexha, David Guetta, Nicki Minaj, Afrojack, G-Eazy, Martin Garrix\n- Works: \"Me, Myself & I\", \"Hey Mama\", \"In the Name of Love\", \"Take Me Home\", I Don't Wanna Grow Up, \"Baby When the Light\", Pop Life\n- Topics: Billboard Hot 100, guest vocals, debut EP, singles\n\nFacts:\n- Bebe Rexha is an American pop recording artist.\n- I Don't Wanna Grow Up is the debut extended play by Bebe Rexha.\n- \"Baby When the Light\" is the third single from Pop Life, the third studio album by David Guetta.\n- Bebe Rexha is best known as a featured guest vocalist on Billboard Hot 100 songs including G-Eazy's \"Me, Myself & I\", David Guetta's \"Hey Mama\", Martin Garrix's \"In the Name of Love\", and Cash Cash's \"Take Me Home\".\n- \"Hey Mama\" is a song by French DJ and record producer David Guetta featuring vocals from Nicki Minaj and Bebe Rexha and production from Dutch DJ and producer Afrojack.",
